  "cause": "**One hundred and twenty legislators from eight parties put their names to a petition on Wednesday demanding the Vice-President's removal, and a resignation offer had already been made in private.** Deputy Speaker **Saan Mustopa** confirmed the petition's submission; under Indonesian law the House leadership must now form a **special committee** to determine whether **Gibran Rakabuming Raka** violated the constitution by serving despite not meeting the requirements for election — after which the matter goes to a court and then to the **MPR**. **Gibran**, the son of former president **Joko Widodo**, told President **Prabowo Subianto** on Tuesday that he intended to resign, according to a presidential official. The trigger is judicial: the **Constitutional Court** and the **Supreme Court** ruled last month that his education documents did not meet election requirements, and the Supreme Court has instructed the education ministry to withdraw his annulled equivalence certificate. Lawmaker **Ahmad Doli Kurnia**: *\"We are requesting the matter to be processed by removing the vice president.\"* The petition is cross-party, and it lands in the middle of a widening rift between **Jokowi** and **Prabowo** — a former president's son and a president's running mate, now a liability to both. **The air over the same country is the other half of the same file, and its official count stopped in July.** Indonesia's environment ministry has not updated burned-area data since **July**, when **202,000 hectares** had burned; the environment group **Auriga** counts more than **637,000 hectares** from January to August — about nine times the area of Singapore — and the deforestation monitor **Nusantara Atlas** puts it near **900,000 hectares**, per **Reuters**. The haze closed schools in Indonesia, **East Timor** and several Malaysian states, including **1,198 schools in Johor** over 8–9 October affecting more than **617,000 students**; nearly **2,000 flights** in Indonesia were affected between 11 August and 12 October; the burning is largely on **peatland**, which converts a millennia-old carbon store into a short-term source. Singapore has warned companies blamed for the haze that its *\"determination to act\"* should not be underestimated; Prabowo has instead berated countries that *\"insult\"* Indonesia over the fires, per **France24**. **And the political number has halved in twelve months.** A **Saiful Mujani Research and Consulting** poll puts Prabowo's approval at **44.5%**, down from **81.2%** in November 2025 and the lowest of any Indonesian president since polling began about twenty years ago, per the **Guardian**. The fires, a weaker economy and the vice-presidential affair are being read as one grievance. Two weeks ago the vice-president's legitimacy was a legal question; this week it is a coalition question, because the 120 signatures come from eight parties — which means the petition is not only an accusation against Gibran but a count of who is willing to be seen standing away from the president.",
  "bullets": [
   "**A resignation offered in private and a petition filed in public cannot both be the settlement** — Gibran told Prabowo on Tuesday he intends to resign; 120 lawmakers filed on Wednesday; the direct effect is that two tracks now compete to define the outcome; the compound consequence is that if he resigns, the signatories get no committee and no findings, and the constitutional question of how he was permitted to run closes without an answer — while if the committee proceeds, a sitting vice-president is adjudicated by a body whose composition is itself a coalition count",
   "**The eligibility ruling is about a certificate, and the precedent is about every future candidate** — the Constitutional Court and Supreme Court finding that education documents did not meet requirements, the ministry instructed to withdraw the equivalence certificate; the direct effect is that a vice-president's mandate is formally in question; the compound consequence is that the entry requirement has been tested once and found meaningless in practice for two years — so the remedy that matters is a published verification standard for candidate documents, applied before ballot printing rather than after inauguration",
   "**A government that stopped counting its own fires cannot win the argument about them** — burned-area data frozen since July, 202,000 hectares official against 637,000 (Auriga) and nearly 900,000 (Nusantara Atlas), haze closing schools in three countries; the direct effect is that the public cannot know the scale of the season it is breathing; the compound consequence is that the gap between the official count and the independent one becomes the political fact — every month of silence is a month in which the outside monitors own the number, and a state that has lost the count has lost the argument about what to do",
   "**Peat is the part of this that is irreversible on any political timetable** — drained peatland burning releases carbon accumulated over thousands of years; the direct effect is emissions no replanting programme offsets within a term of office; the compound consequence is that a concession map overlapping **3.68 million hectares** of logging and mining permits with key biodiversity areas guarantees the next fire season — so approval ratings and fire seasons now move on the same cycle, and each dry year costs the incumbent what the last one cost him",
   "**A succession question inside a coalition is settled by arithmetic, and arithmetic is not a constitutional procedure** — eight parties, 120 signatures, an MPR vote downstream, a president at a two-decade low; the direct effect is that every party prices its position against the next election rather than the current law; the compound consequence is that the vice-presidency becomes vacant or contested precisely when the government must legislate a fire-and-haze budget — and a weakened executive cannot enforce a concession moratorium against the interests that fund its coalition"
  ],
  "verse": "Through your self-acquired characteristic of concentrating solely on the material you human beings of Earth have effectively made yourselves to masters of your coarse-substantial world, and as a result of your doing, handling and acting, the material world has also become dependent on you; but you use this dependence of your world to torment it in every imaginable wise, for example through chemistry, irresponsible exploitation of the resources, through overpopulation and the immense resultant problems which can no longer be solved, such as the destruction of the climate, mass migrations, water and food scarcity, hatred, war, torture and the destruction of the environment and nature, the eradication of many animal, bird and fish species etc.; for better or for worse, your world has become dependent on you and perforce suffers in its own kind and wise under your terror and through the destructions which you cause upon it and to it.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 28, Verse 150",
  "hinge": "§28:150 names the mechanism precisely — the world has become *dependent* on human handling, and that dependence is being used to torment it, through *irresponsible exploitation of the resources*. The next verse is the instruction: *\"It is you alone who can raise your Earth again, if you stop with all your terror and with your destructions.\"* Applied here, the change is not a rescue operation but a publication schedule, and it is available this week: monthly burned-area releases with the concession names attached, health thresholds that trigger school closures automatically rather than diplomatically, and candidate-eligibility verification published before nomination papers are accepted. The first two answer the air; the third answers the vice-president. Each substitutes a number the public can check for a discretion the public cannot. A state that resumes counting is a state that can still be argued with."
